FlyOps connectome data: FlyWire FAFB v783 whole-brain connectome
=================================================================

Completeness_783.csv, Connectivity_783.parquet
  Source: https://github.com/philshiu/Drosophila_brain_model (commit 91bdd1e7dcf193f3e7ca5a8933497fcef63b7960)
  License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Philip Shiu and Nico Spiller
  Derived from the FlyWire connectome (https://flywire.ai), materialization 783, whose connectivity release is
  licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10676866, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

mapping.json
  Generated by FlyOps (hack/flywire_mapping.py) from the cell-type annotations published with Schlegel et al.,
  Nature 634:139 (2024), licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07686-5), as distributed in
  https://github.com/flyconnectome/flywire_annotations (tag v2.1.0, "the version reported on in Schlegel et al.").
  Only neuron root IDs grouped by FlyOps channel/population are included, not the annotation file.
  Changes: cell types were selected and grouped by FlyOps; the grouping is engineering, not biology.

Please cite when using this data:
  Dorkenwald et al. (2024) Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain. Nature 634, 124-138.
  Schlegel et al. (2024) Whole-brain annotation and multi-connectome cell typing of Drosophila. Nature 634, 139-152.
  Shiu et al. (2024) A Drosophila computational brain model reveals sensorimotor processing. Nature 634, 210-219.

The simulator in FlyOps is a Rust re-implementation of the Shiu et al. leaky integrate-and-fire model. It has not
been validated against the upstream Brian2 simulator.
